// Regression: display <-> protocols was a direct module cycle.
//
// protocols.hv imported display (for its lazy X connection) while
// display.hv imported protocols (for getWindowProp/getStringProp). The cycle
// only fired when display was reached through a third module first:
// `use display` alone succeeded, but
//     use display
//     use mode          // mode -> window -> display -> protocols -> display
// died at shutdown with
//     Execution error: Circular dependency detected: protocols
// because by then the display module was already in-progress and could not be
// re-entered.
//
// protocols now opens its own connection through x11 (XOpenDisplay(NULL),
// i.e. $DISPLAY) and caches it, so the edge protocols -> display is gone.
// display still passes its own _dpy in explicitly, so nothing else changed.
//
// The pairs below each failed before the fix; headless-safe (module load only,
// no display is opened).

use display
use mode

print "PASS: display_mode_no_cycle"
process.exit(0)